# Cursor Rules for DayMatch

## Project Context
DayMatch is a short-term job matching platform (단기 알바 매칭 플랫폼) connecting employers with workers for daily/temporary jobs.

## Tech Stack
- **Backend**: NestJS 10.x + TypeScript + TypeORM + PostgreSQL
- **Mobile**: React Native (Expo SDK 50+) + Redux Toolkit
- **Admin**: React + Vite + Tailwind CSS
- **Infrastructure**: Railway (Backend), Vercel (Admin), EAS (Mobile)

## Code Style

### TypeScript
- Use strict mode (strict: true)
- Explicit return types on all functions
- No `any` - use `unknown` with type guards
- Use absolute imports with @/ prefix

### NestJS Backend
- Controller → Service → Repository pattern
- All DTOs must have class-validator decorators
- Swagger decorators on all endpoints
- Use Guards for auth/authz

### React/React Native
- Functional components with hooks only
- Redux Toolkit with createSlice
- RTK Query for API calls

## Naming Conventions
- Files: `kebab-case.ts` or `PascalCase.tsx`
- Classes: `PascalCase`
- Functions/Variables: `camelCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- DB Columns: `snake_case`

## File Structure
```
backend/src/
├── auth/           # Authentication (JWT, OAuth)
├── users/          # User management
├── jobs/           # Job CRUD
├── applications/   # Application management
├── matches/        # Match management
├── payments/       # Payment (TossPayments)
├── chats/          # Real-time chat
├── notifications/  # Push notifications
├── reviews/        # Reviews/Ratings
└── common/         # Shared utilities

mobile/src/
├── screens/        # Screen components
├── components/     # Reusable components
├── store/          # Redux store
├── services/       # API services
└── hooks/          # Custom hooks

admin/src/
├── pages/          # Page components
├── components/     # UI components
└── services/       # API services
```

## Don't
- Don't use class components in React
- Don't use CSS modules (use Tailwind)
- Don't add unnecessary dependencies
- Don't commit .env files
- Don't use `any` type

## Commands
```bash
npm run verify      # typecheck + lint + build
npm run typecheck   # TypeScript check
npm run lint        # ESLint check
```

## Important Files
- `CLAUDE.md` - Full project context
- `docs/adr/` - Architecture decisions
- `docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md` - Common issues
